{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.9,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U41", "U44"],
      "pins": ["U41.5", "U44.5", "U41.4", "U44.4"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "The isolated CAN transceivers U41 and U44 have their isolated-side ground pins (GND2, pin 5) tied directly to the common logic ground net GND, the same net as their logic-side ground pins (GND1, pin 4).",
      "expected": "For an isolated CAN transceiver, GND2 must connect to an isolated ground net separate from GND1 to maintain galvanic isolation between the CAN bus and the logic side.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U41\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U44\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (U8, U9) through an isolated CAN transceiver (U11/companion)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The isolation barrier is shorted, so the CAN buses are not galvanically isolated. This defeats the intended isolation, risking ground loops, noise, and damage between the rover's logic and motor controllers.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["U17", "R1", "U39", "Q9"],
      "pins": ["U17.2", "U17.4", "U39.5", "Q9.1"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "/NET0086"],
      "observed": "U17 is an SN74LVC1G07 open-drain buffer. Its input pin A (pin 2) is tied to the +3V3 supply, so its output Y (pin 4) is always high-impedance. The net /NET0086 is pulled low by R1 (10k to GND) and drives the enable pin of the WS2812 level shifter U39 and the gate of the WS2812 ground switch Q9.",
      "expected": "U17's input should be driven by a control signal so that it can pull /NET0086 low when the WS2812 LEDs are to be enabled. With A tied high, /NET0086 is permanently low, disabling U39 and Q9.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U17\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U17\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"Y\") (pintype \"output\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R1\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Addressable status LEDs (WS2812B, D5-D7, D18-D21) and an analog switch (ISL54222AIUZ, U5) for LED/signal routing."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "All WS2812B addressable status LEDs are permanently disabled because their level shifter and ground switch are held off. The board cannot display status via these LEDs.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_supply",
      "components": ["U11", "U6"],
      "pins": ["U11.15", "U11.3", "U11.13", "U6.2"],
      "nets": ["+3V3"],
      "observed": "The FT231XS USB-UART bridge U11 has its VCC pin (pin 15) and VCCIO pin (pin 3) tied to the +3V3 rail. Its internal 3.3V LDO output 3V3OUT (pin 13) is also tied to the same +3V3 rail, which is simultaneously driven by the board's 3.3V LDO U6 (TLV1117LV33).",
      "expected": "The FT231XS VCC pin requires a 5V supply (datasheet range 4.0–5.5V). The 3V3OUT pin is an output and must not be connected to an external 3.3V rail that is already driven by another regulator; it should be left unconnected or used only for VCCIO if VCC is 5V.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"15\") (pinfunction \"VCC\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"3V3OUT\") (pintype \"power_out\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"VO\") (pintype \"power_out\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The FT231XS is powered from an out-of-spec 3.3V rail, and its internal LDO output fights the board's 3.3V regulator. This can prevent USB enumeration, damage the FT231XS or U6, and cause instability on the +3V3 rail.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies. The most critical is that the isolated CAN transceivers U41 and U44 have their isolated grounds tied to common GND, defeating the required galvanic isolation. Additionally, U17 is miswired so the WS2812 status LEDs are permanently disabled, and the FT231XS USB-UART bridge is powered from 3.3V with its internal LDO output shorted to the board's 3.3V rail."
}

